    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Coins, stones, seashells, toys, and stamps are among the many collectible items. You name it; someone collects it. What "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " people to collect things? One important reason is that it’s fun. No matter what else is going on in your life, if you’re a collector, you can set yourself clear goals. You can enjoy the “"
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” for the next item on your wish list. After that, just enjoy adding new items to your collection. You can also find "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in showing it to others."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In fact, the social side of collecting is also an important part of its "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "charm",
            "ref": "v-charm"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Collectors often form communities, share knowledge, or "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with each other. This gives them a strong sense of belonging. The internet has made it easier for these kinds of communities to develop."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Other collectors collect things because of "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "nostalgia",
            "ref": "v-nostalgia"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". For example, some people collect items from "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " because they want to preserve aspects of bygone eras. Think of the person collecting Ming Dynasty vases."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Some items might hold "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " memories. For example, some people were crazy about certain things when they were little. They might revisit their childhood passions in later life. For these people, their "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " acts as a safety net from the adult world. It allows them to momentarily escape the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "burdens",
            "ref": "v-burden"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of their present lives and reconnect with their "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " selves."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Some "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "psychologists",
            "zh": "心理学家"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " argue that there are even deeper reasons behind collecting. They say that the "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of collecting can "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "stem from",
            "ref": "v-stem-from"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a lack of loving human relationships. The collection can "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " missing connections. For some people, collecting things can also be a way to deal with "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "existential anxieties",
            "zh": "存在焦虑"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
